[size=6][b]ABIOTIC EDITOR[/b][/size]
[size=4][i]The friendly save editor for Abiotic Factor.[/i][/size]

[b]Steam[/b] and [b]Game Pass / Microsoft Store[/b] saves, [b]single-player[/b] and [b]dedicated servers[/b]. Windows, Linux, Steam Deck and macOS. No hex editor, no spreadsheets.

[size=5][b]▶ Try it right now, in your browser: [url=https://christophervr.github.io/AbioticEditor/app/]christophervr.github.io/AbioticEditor/app[/url][/b][/size]
[i]Nothing to download. Your saves never leave your computer.[/i][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b]What is this?[/b][/size]

Abiotic Factor keeps your progress in save files on your PC. Abiotic Editor opens those files and shows everything inside as simple controls: sliders for your needs, a grid for your inventory, a checklist for recipes, and a 3D view of your base. Change what you want, press SAVE, and load the game.

It reads the game's own data from your installed copy, so you see your real item pictures, recipe names, skill perks, story text and even the game's 3D models. Nothing from the game is in the download.

It is a fan-made tool and is not part of the game.

[center][img]https://christophervr.github.io/AbioticEditor/screenshots/50-3d-view.png[/img]
[i]Your base in the 3D view, drawn with the game's own models. Click any piece to see and change it.[/i][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b]What can I do with it?[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Your character:[/b] top up hunger, thirst, sanity and health, max a skill, give yourself money, unlock recipes, hand yourself any item, change traits, looks, transmog and respawn point.
[*][b]Your world:[/b] restock containers, open doors, recover dropped items, revive a story character, look after pets, fix vehicles, set story progress, unlock traders, fill containment cells, and tend garden plots and chemistry benches.
[*][b]Your base, in 3D:[/b] walk through it, move and copy pieces, place new ones from a picture palette, and wire up power.
[*][b]Fix a mistake:[/b] refill a node you harvested, repair a broken window or ice wall, or put the story back in order.
[*][b]Move between worlds and platforms:[/b] move items between saves, and convert a world between Game Pass and Steam in either direction.
[*][b]Run a server:[/b] edit any player's save, change world state, or adjust difficulty and rates without touching a text file.
[*][b]Change a running game:[/b] live editing applies changes while you play. See below.
[/list]

